  "source_recovery": {
    "IK-55384096:L67:span1": {
      "text": "The case of the petitioner was that a shop on the ground floor of property bearing no.95, Main Bazar, Najafgarh, Delhi which had been let out to the original tenant Hakim Rai and which had since been sublet by him in favour of his son-in-law Raj Kumar; Hakim Rai had divested himself completely from the suit property.",
      "document_id": "55384096",
      "url": "https://indiankanoon.org/doc/55384096/",
      "semantic_stage": "PRE_TARGET_RECORD",
      "prospective_availability": "RETROSPECTIVELY_RECONSTRUCTED_PRE_TARGET"
    },
    "IK-55384096:L70:span3": {
      "text": "A partnership deed dated 20.11.1983 (Ex.AW-3/13) has been executed between the father-in-law, Hakim Rai and his son-in-law, Raj Kumar to the aforenoted effect wherein the parties had agreed that the business under the said partnership would be conducted from the suit premises.",
      "document_id": "55384096",
      "url": "https://indiankanoon.org/doc/55384096/",
      "semantic_stage": "PRE_TARGET_RECORD",
      "prospective_availability": "RETROSPECTIVELY_RECONSTRUCTED_PRE_TARGET"
    },
    "IK-55384096:L71:span4": {
      "text": "contention of the landlord, however, is that this partnership deed was a fake CM(M) No.1574/2010 Page 2 of 10 and forged document and had been created only as a sham defence to the present eviction petition under cite12†Section 14(1)(b) of the DRCA",
      "document_id": "55384096",
      "url": "https://indiankanoon.org/doc/55384096/",
      "semantic_stage": "PRE_TARGET_RECORD",
      "prospective_availability": "RETROSPECTIVELY_RECONSTRUCTED_PRE_TARGET"
    },
    "IK-55384096:L77:span5": {
      "text": "she denied the CM(M) No.1574/2010 Page 4 of 10 suggestion that her husband was no longer in possession or in the business after the induction of Raj Kumar",
      "document_id": "55384096",
      "url": "https://indiankanoon.org/doc/55384096/",
      "semantic_stage": "PRE_TARGET_RECORD",
      "prospective_availability": "RETROSPECTIVELY_RECONSTRUCTED_PRE_TARGET"
    },
    "IK-55384096:L77:span6": {
      "text": "she had also admitted that Raj Kumar was partner in the business of her husband in the demised shop",
      "document_id": "55384096",
      "url": "https://indiankanoon.org/doc/55384096/",
      "semantic_stage": "PRE_TARGET_RECORD",
      "prospective_availability": "RETROSPECTIVELY_RECONSTRUCTED_PRE_TARGET"
    },
    "IK-55384096:L79:span7": {
      "text": "the son-in- law (Raj Kumar) and father-in-law (Hakim Rai) are residing in the same premises and ration card of Raj Kumar has been obtained at the same address. The partnership deed Ex.AW-3/13 had been executed between the parties in November, 1983",
      "document_id": "55384096",
      "url": "https://indiankanoon.org/doc/55384096/",
      "semantic_stage": "PRE_TARGET_RECORD",
      "prospective_availability": "RETROSPECTIVELY_RECONSTRUCTED_PRE_TARGET"
    },
    "IK-55384096:L69:span2": {
      "text": "The defence set up by Hakim Rai (tenant) was that he was old, aged, ailing and had lost his eyesight. In the last part of the year 1983 he had requested his son-in-law to assist him in his business",
      "document_id": "55384096",
      "url": "https://indiankanoon.org/doc/55384096/",
      "semantic_stage": "PRE_TARGET_RECORD",
      "prospective_availability": "RETROSPECTIVELY_RECONSTRUCTED_PRE_TARGET"
    },
    "IK-55384096:L80:span8": {
      "text": "The attorney of the landlord PW-3 has also admitted that the respondent Hakim Rai is an old man; he has very poor eyesight and cannot even walk properly.",
      "document_id": "55384096",
      "url": "https://indiankanoon.org/doc/55384096/",
      "semantic_stage": "PRE_TARGET_RECORD",
      "prospective_availability": "RETROSPECTIVELY_RECONSTRUCTED_PRE_TARGET"
    }
  },
